<poml>
  <task>Decide how to handle the user's latest message, then respond only with a JSON object.</task>
  <instructions>Set "intent" to "conversational" when the message is social or about yourself and needs no work, research, or data: greetings, thanks, small talk, questions about who you are or what you can do, and similar. Set "intent" to "task" for anything that asks for information, analysis, a decision, or an action.
When "intent" is "conversational", put your complete reply to the user in "reply". When "intent" is "task", set "reply" to an empty string; the full answer is written in a later step.
Set "document" when the user asks for a deliverable to keep: a document, report, brief, proposal, plan, specification, write-up, or file, including revisions of an existing document. Give it a short, specific title and an integer imageCount from zero to six. If the user asks for images, illustrations, diagrams, visual explanations, or image-based flowcharts in that document, imageCount must be at least one and must respect any specified count up to six. Choose useful visuals where they materially improve the requested document, even when the user does not prescribe their exact form. Requests for more than six images exceed one document's supported generation limit; do not silently reduce the requested number. Otherwise set "document" to null.</instructions>
  <output-format>A single JSON object and nothing else: {"intent": "conversational" or "task", "reply": "your reply or an empty string", "document": {"title": "document title", "imageCount": 0} or null, "delegate": [{"name": "exact teammate name", "task": "what that teammate should contribute"}]}</output-format>
</poml>
